<p>mmmmrm</p>
<p>This is a neutral vote on my part. There are some wonky areas where the formality of the writing overtakes the functionality (&quot; until such a time as a Berliner event spontaneously occurs,&quot; &quot;an SCP-1681-1 instance (one Boleslava Medvedeva)&quot;). In regards to the idea itself, I'm&#8230;bluh, honestly, I really have no idea what I'm supposed to be getting out of this. Is it supposed to be funny? Should I be laughing? Is it, like, scary? People bursting into bald eagles is not scary. It's absurd, and I get the feeling that this whole thing is supposed to be really absurd and that's why I should upvote, but there's nothing really interesting behind the absurdity. Like, the only real thing I can see behind the absurdity is the stereotypical &quot;capitalist pigdog&quot; strain of humor. Which doesn't particularly make me want to upvote.</p>

