<p>Now see, I <em>want</em> people to go 'What the hell is that?' and Google it. You're also the umpteenth person to remark on this, so I'll relent. ;)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Bald eagles are not small birds. How does one accidentally ingest a bald eagle? (Admittedly, I may not want to know the answer to this.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's exactly what I'm going for. I'm not entirely sure either, but it's bound to be messy.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>MTF should probably be spelled out as Mobile Task Force the first time it's used in a document, just for clinicality's sake.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Noted.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>MTF Chi-3 is one of the example task forces in Task Forces. While you're certainly not obligated to change this, I did spend a lot of time making sure that nothing on that guide clashed with existing usage. :)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Dammit. I always check whether I'm going to do something that conflicts with established canon. I'll edit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A significant amount of time was spent trying to ensure that the various nicknames for the example task forces were suitably conversational, meaning that it's reasonably non-silly to say things like, &quot;we need to call in the Exorcists&quot; or &quot;it's already being handled by the Debuggers&quot;. &quot;Mops and Buckets&quot; doesn't lend itself to casual usage very well.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Aww&#8230;I like &quot;Mop and Bucket&quot;. :( Will edit though, in light of the next point.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Very minor personal point as well, it seems really strange for two separate Mobile Task Forces to be mobilized for a single SCP; what's the point of a specialized task force if it can only monitor or handle a situation, but not both? Another option is that Foundation field agents across the world monitor for emergence, but a task force is responsible for handling it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You're probably right.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;auditory memetic cognitohazard&quot; is a bit weird, since &quot;memetic agent&quot; already implies &quot;cognitohazard&quot;. By common usage, &quot;auditory memetic agent&quot; works just fine.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Motherfucker, I knew it. This is my first attempt at a memetic threat and I listened to someone who told me &quot;auditory memetic agent&quot; wasn't enough. :|</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All memetic agents are self-propagating. Did you mean &quot;spontaneous outbreak&quot; instead?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yup, you got me.</p>
<p>All in all, good points. Thanks, Aelanna. :)</p>

